outputs.L1:
The invention relates to a method for producing and/or capturing neutrons, comprising the following steps:

a) exposing nuclei selected from among protons, deuterons and/or tritons to an electric field in order to extract said nuclei and to direct the nuclei thus extracted towards a target (20) containing free electrons;

b) optionally, exposing said nuclei to a spatial and/or temporal gradient of a first magnetic field so as to impart a predefined orientation to the magnetic moments of the nuclei;

c) either exposing the target to a second magnetic field so as to impart a predefined orientation to the magnetic moments of the free electrons of the target;

d) or employing an electron-donor superparamagnetic material, such that the electrons of the free layers of these materials are oriented along preferred directions generated by the orientation of the resulting magnetic moment of the superparamagnetic material;

e) optionally, in the case where a superparamagnetic material is employed, refraining from exposing the proton beam and/or the target to external magnetic fields.

A heating device and/or a device for generating magnetic fields may be required in order to activate the superparamagnetic properties of the material.

outputs.L2:
This invention pertains to a technique for generating and/or capturing neutrons, comprising the steps outlined below:

a) Subjecting nuclei—chosen from among protons, deuterons and/or tritons—to an electric field, thereby drawing out these nuclei and steering them toward a target (20) that holds free electrons;

b) As an illustration, subjecting these nuclei to a gradient—whether spatial and/or temporal—of an initial magnetic field, thereby establishing a predetermined alignment of the nuclei's magnetic moments;

c) Either subjecting the target to a secondary magnetic field, thereby establishing a predetermined alignment of the magnetic moments belonging to the target's free electrons;

d) Or alternatively employing a superparamagnetic material that donates electrons, such that the electrons in the free layers of these materials become aligned along favored directions produced by how the overall magnetic moment of the superparamagnetic material is oriented;

e) As an illustration, when a superparamagnetic material is employed, refraining from subjecting the proton beam and/or the target to any external magnetic fields.

To trigger the superparamagnetic characteristics of the material, it may become necessary to use a heating apparatus and/or an apparatus that produces magnetic fields.
